WEBVTT

00:17.392 --> 00:19.560
‎Joseph of Arimathea

00:19.561 --> 00:23.439
‎took Jesus Christ down
‎from the cross at Golgotha.

00:23.440 --> 00:26.443
‎He cleansed his body and laid him to rest.

00:27.360 --> 00:31.156
‎He later became a missionary
‎and set out on a journey.

00:32.449 --> 00:34.408
‎His journey led him to Britannia,

00:34.409 --> 00:38.203
‎the northern isle
‎where the British Empire would later rise.

00:38.204 --> 00:40.290
‎There, he built a church.

00:41.291 --> 00:45.420
‎And there, he drew a map
‎no one could understand.

00:46.212 --> 00:48.922
‎No one recognized
‎its coastlines, landforms,

00:48.923 --> 00:50.591
‎or where it depicted.

00:50.592 --> 00:54.596
‎Joseph himself died
‎without ever explaining it.

00:57.432 --> 01:00.059
‎In 1184,

01:00.060 --> 01:04.272
‎a fire broke out at Glastonbury Abbey,
‎built atop the church's ruins.

01:04.898 --> 01:08.193
‎A single parchment
‎was found among the ashes.

01:09.152 --> 01:14.407
‎It proved to be
‎Joseph of Arimathea's lost map.

01:14.991 --> 01:17.993
‎What had Joseph sought?

01:17.994 --> 01:19.828
‎What land did it depict?

01:19.829 --> 01:22.373
‎No one ever knew.

01:22.999 --> 01:27.002
‎Then, as the 16th century dawned,

01:27.003 --> 01:32.509
‎Joseph's map was stolen
‎and disappeared from Glastonbury.

01:33.092 --> 01:38.223
‎It happened a couple of years after
‎the discovery of the New World, America.

01:39.307 --> 01:40.433
‎And then...

01:41.184 --> 01:44.187
‎The year was 1890!

01:47.440 --> 01:49.316
‎What the hell is this?

01:49.317 --> 01:50.943
‎Gyro!

01:50.944 --> 01:53.362
‎Wait! Wait up!

01:53.363 --> 01:56.615
‎My left hand! What's happening?

01:56.616 --> 01:59.202
‎Look!

02:07.127 --> 02:08.961
‎What the hell?

02:08.962 --> 02:10.712
‎Hey, what's your problem?

02:10.713 --> 02:14.883
‎You call for me,
‎then ignore me and talk to the ground?

02:14.884 --> 02:17.469
‎No! There's something there!

02:17.470 --> 02:20.305
‎Something just went into my hand!

02:20.306 --> 02:23.934
‎It came out of my left hand,
‎then went back in!

02:23.935 --> 02:25.562
‎Are you hurt?

02:27.021 --> 02:28.022
‎No...

02:28.773 --> 02:32.776
‎A hallucination? No, that's not it.

02:32.777 --> 02:36.531
‎It's not a hallucination
‎or a Stand ability.

02:37.365 --> 02:41.118
‎Making my nails spin at will...

02:41.119 --> 02:43.036
‎That's my Stand ability.

02:43.037 --> 02:46.291
‎But my hand... This is different.

02:47.000 --> 02:48.542
‎It feels different.

02:48.543 --> 02:50.294
‎There's something in there.

02:50.295 --> 02:54.132
‎There's someone else's left hand
‎inside mine!

02:54.924 --> 02:57.051
‎But... since when?

03:11.691 --> 03:13.818
‎JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE

04:28.434 --> 04:32.188
‎TUSK, PART 1

04:32.772 --> 04:37.567
‎That photo was taken
‎by Balloon No. 3 from 600 feet up.

04:37.568 --> 04:41.154
‎523 racers dropped out there.

04:41.155 --> 04:44.241
‎The death toll stands at 68.

04:44.242 --> 04:47.119
‎Too many. All from that area?

04:47.120 --> 04:48.287
‎Yes, sir.

04:48.288 --> 04:52.499
‎Most appear to have been unhorsed
‎by the quicksand.

04:52.500 --> 04:54.418
‎According to the local Apache,

04:54.419 --> 04:59.381
‎this land...
‎They call it the "Devil's Palm."

04:59.382 --> 05:01.049
‎It shifts like quicksand,

05:01.050 --> 05:04.304
‎and no one can predict
‎where it'll appear next.

05:04.887 --> 05:08.266
‎The place in the photo disappeared
‎six or seven hours later.

05:09.058 --> 05:13.937
‎Geologists believe it's connected
‎to an ancient meteor impact,

05:13.938 --> 05:17.858
‎but why it moves like a living thing
‎remains a mystery.

05:17.859 --> 05:21.653
‎The Apache believe that approaching it
‎brings misfortune.

05:21.654 --> 05:23.114
‎They have a saying...

05:24.324 --> 05:28.077
‎"The Devil's Palm chooses the people."

05:39.589 --> 05:43.050
‎Was Gyro Zeppeli the first
‎to pass through this land?

05:43.051 --> 05:46.762
‎Yes, sir. The balloons
‎have lost sight of him.

05:46.763 --> 05:49.056
‎But Gyro Zeppeli still leads,

05:49.057 --> 05:51.142
‎with Johnny Joestar alongside him.

05:51.726 --> 05:55.438
‎They appear to be about 12 miles
‎from the finish at Monument Valley.

05:56.898 --> 06:00.901
‎After Gyro Zeppeli
‎passed through the Devil's Palm...

06:00.902 --> 06:04.697
‎Did anyone see him find anything?

06:05.823 --> 06:07.658
‎Such as...

06:09.577 --> 06:10.995
‎Mr. Steel?

06:11.704 --> 06:14.623
‎A corpse, for example.

06:14.624 --> 06:19.087
‎It's possible he found a human corpse
‎in this land.

06:20.838 --> 06:24.467
‎He may be hiding it
‎in his bags or his tack. Find out.

06:25.635 --> 06:29.179
‎Sorry, could you repeat that?

06:29.180 --> 06:31.474
‎I don't mean an entire corpse.

06:32.058 --> 06:35.685
‎It could be just a body part,
‎like a hand or a leg.

06:35.686 --> 06:38.106
‎It may even be mummified.

06:38.648 --> 06:41.526
‎Have the balloons search from the air!

06:42.860 --> 06:44.028
‎This is rather sudden...

06:44.779 --> 06:49.616
‎Mr. Steel. Is there another reason
‎you're determined

06:49.617 --> 06:51.536
‎to make this race a success?

06:52.286 --> 06:55.915
‎Just whose corpse could it be?

06:56.874 --> 06:59.126
‎Let me be perfectly clear.

06:59.127 --> 07:03.421
‎We will make the Steel Ball Run a success,
‎no matter what.

07:03.422 --> 07:05.133
‎That is our only objective.

07:05.716 --> 07:09.929
‎But for now, your only job
‎is to investigate Gyro Zeppeli.

07:10.930 --> 07:12.223
‎Yes, sir.

07:13.599 --> 07:15.059
‎Excuse me.

07:20.982 --> 07:24.068
‎Let me correct one thing, Mr. Steel.

07:25.153 --> 07:27.154
‎It's not just "possible."

07:27.155 --> 07:29.531
‎Gyro Zeppeli has found it.

07:29.532 --> 07:31.575
‎At the Devil's Palm.

07:31.576 --> 07:34.327
‎I'm 100% certain.

07:34.328 --> 07:36.831
‎Gyro Zeppeli found the corpse.

07:38.499 --> 07:44.421
‎The man we sent, Oye,
‎left a message at the checkpoint.

07:44.422 --> 07:48.800
‎Unfortunately, he was defeated
‎before he could take the corpse.

07:48.801 --> 07:53.306
‎So Gyro Zeppeli's after the corpse,
‎just like we are?

07:55.224 --> 07:57.934
‎We don't know yet.

07:57.935 --> 08:01.813
‎He may have found it by chance
‎during the race.

08:01.814 --> 08:05.817
‎Or he may not even realize
‎he's found it yet.

08:05.818 --> 08:10.281
‎That's the nature of the corpse
‎and the Devil's Palm.

08:11.157 --> 08:13.159
‎The corpse chooses the person!

08:14.118 --> 08:17.412
‎The important thing here

08:17.413 --> 08:20.790
‎is that the corpse won't disappear
‎after Gyro is eliminated.

08:20.791 --> 08:27.215
‎To do that, we must determine
‎how and where he's carrying it.

08:28.508 --> 08:31.927
‎Wait a minute! Eliminate Gyro Zeppeli?

08:31.928 --> 08:34.596
‎I agreed to cooperate fully,

08:34.597 --> 08:38.433
‎but no one said
‎there'd be murder in my race!

08:38.434 --> 08:40.268
‎I thought we were
‎just looking for the corpse!

08:40.269 --> 08:41.854
‎Listen carefully, Mr. Steel.

08:42.688 --> 08:45.774
‎Obtaining that corpse is justice!

08:45.775 --> 08:47.818
‎We'll use whatever means are necessary!

08:48.861 --> 08:52.155
‎Humanity has long sought that corpse
‎more than any power

08:52.156 --> 08:54.367
‎or treasure in history.

08:55.034 --> 08:59.121
‎In the end, we'll have it for sure!

09:08.256 --> 09:11.509
‎Make the Steel Ball Run a success.

09:12.260 --> 09:14.971
‎A race that follows the route
‎marked on this map.

09:15.555 --> 09:18.974
‎If someone with the ability
‎follows this route,

09:18.975 --> 09:21.811
‎they will surely
‎gather the scattered corpse parts.

09:23.521 --> 09:26.690
‎And then... "Murder"?

09:26.691 --> 09:29.026
‎Choose your words carefully, Steven Steel.

09:29.819 --> 09:34.865
‎Without me, this race
‎would never have happened.

09:39.662 --> 09:40.997
‎Understood.

09:41.706 --> 09:43.499
‎President...

09:44.292 --> 09:45.835
‎of the United States.

09:49.213 --> 09:50.839
‎Excuse me. I brought coffee.

09:50.840 --> 09:53.843
‎Don't come in!
‎You're not cleared to enter!

09:59.932 --> 10:01.600
‎Mr. President!

10:01.601 --> 10:04.144
‎My deepest apologies. This is my wife.

10:04.145 --> 10:05.813
‎She doesn't know any better...

10:10.818 --> 10:12.111
‎Be careful.

10:12.862 --> 10:15.822
‎Yes, sir! My sincerest apologies...

10:15.823 --> 10:17.407
‎Not me.

10:17.408 --> 10:21.202
‎Your young, beautiful wife.

10:21.203 --> 10:22.413
‎Above her head.

10:35.426 --> 10:37.927
‎What my men carry out,

10:37.928 --> 10:39.096
‎Mr. Steel,

10:39.722 --> 10:41.848
‎is an operation.

10:41.849 --> 10:43.683
‎Not murder.

10:43.684 --> 10:46.812
‎Not when they act on my orders!

10:52.443 --> 10:53.486
‎On the roof...

10:54.570 --> 10:56.447
‎Is that a person?

10:57.406 --> 10:58.949
‎How is that possible?

10:59.575 --> 11:01.243
‎It spilled...

11:01.744 --> 11:03.162
‎but nothing's wet.

11:04.038 --> 11:05.247
‎Where's the coffee?

11:08.501 --> 11:13.213
‎Hey, Johnny.
‎Have you ever been to an opera?

11:13.214 --> 11:14.714
‎An opera.

11:14.715 --> 11:17.050
‎An opera? That music thing?

11:17.051 --> 11:20.011
‎The kind of play
‎where they could just say the lines,

11:20.012 --> 11:23.515
‎but suddenly start singing
‎to explain the situation instead?

11:23.516 --> 11:24.558
‎What else?

11:25.142 --> 11:27.769
‎No, but why do you ask?

11:27.770 --> 11:29.396
‎Just curious.

11:29.397 --> 11:32.607
‎They're called opera glasses
‎because they're for opera, right?

11:32.608 --> 11:35.777
‎But those singers on the stage...

11:35.778 --> 11:37.695
‎They're huge, aren't they?

11:37.696 --> 11:40.698
‎That's probably
‎why they've got such powerful voices.

11:40.699 --> 11:44.327
‎So why use opera glasses to look at them?

11:44.328 --> 11:47.206
‎You don't need opera glasses.
‎The singers are huge.

11:48.290 --> 11:54.170
‎What, to see if the buttons
‎on their fancy costumes are about to pop?

11:54.171 --> 11:56.424
‎True. You've got a point.

11:56.924 --> 12:02.221
‎Or because they all have the same build,
‎you have to get a closer look?

12:04.056 --> 12:06.058
‎Johnny! That's a good one!

12:08.727 --> 12:11.354
‎Look, Gyro. That's Monument Valley.

12:11.355 --> 12:13.440
‎We're an hour or two from the finish.

12:13.441 --> 12:15.108
‎Should we pick up the pace?

12:15.109 --> 12:17.360
‎No. We'll keep this pace.

12:17.361 --> 12:19.280
‎We can still take first.

12:49.143 --> 12:50.186
‎Gyro?

13:01.822 --> 13:03.616
‎Gyro! Where are you?

13:04.366 --> 13:05.367
‎Gyro!

13:11.332 --> 13:13.042
‎Did he fall off his horse?

13:13.751 --> 13:14.752
‎No way!

13:16.003 --> 13:17.795
‎Gyro! Answer me!

13:17.796 --> 13:20.798
‎Where are you, Gyro?

13:20.799 --> 13:21.800
‎Gyro!

13:23.219 --> 13:24.428
‎Gyro!

13:27.014 --> 13:28.057
‎Gyro!

13:34.939 --> 13:37.524
‎An enemy... We're under attack.

13:37.525 --> 13:40.903
‎His horse...
‎Only Gyro's horse disappeared.

13:41.403 --> 13:42.905
‎But how?

13:44.198 --> 13:45.491
‎Gyro!

13:46.617 --> 13:48.994
‎Where are you, Gyro?

13:49.703 --> 13:51.330
‎Answer me!

14:01.590 --> 14:04.677
‎What is this? Even his gear is gone!

14:06.554 --> 14:08.472
‎It's all disappearing!

14:11.016 --> 14:12.184
‎What?

14:14.395 --> 14:17.731
‎The enemy's above us!
‎Somehow, it's overhead!

14:20.818 --> 14:23.403
‎What kind of power is this?

14:23.404 --> 14:25.698
‎What's up there?

14:38.544 --> 14:41.463
‎It's a Stand User!

14:44.216 --> 14:46.384
‎I'm a target too!

14:46.385 --> 14:49.220
‎Gyro isn't their only target.

14:49.221 --> 14:51.222
‎Just as I thought,

14:51.223 --> 14:54.101
‎this race was never
‎just about winning or losing!

15:00.733 --> 15:02.610
‎My horse too!

15:03.402 --> 15:05.279
‎Damn it! How's that possible?

15:05.863 --> 15:08.115
‎Where is it? What's there?

15:21.754 --> 15:23.881
‎What's this?

15:24.840 --> 15:27.176
‎The feather... It's coming from inside!

15:32.056 --> 15:33.265
‎I can't cut it!

15:44.318 --> 15:45.861
‎A Stand ability!

15:46.570 --> 15:50.115
‎So that feather connects to another space?

15:51.367 --> 15:54.995
‎Gyro and his horse
‎were snagged by those hooks...

16:03.963 --> 16:05.505
‎They're after me!

16:05.506 --> 16:08.217
‎They're trying to snag me!

16:09.510 --> 16:12.471
‎It's hollow under that rock. That'll work!

16:13.055 --> 16:16.892
‎Anyway, I've got to hide under there!

17:11.947 --> 17:14.699
‎It's above me. Right above me.

17:14.700 --> 17:17.828
‎This enemy is determined to kill me.

17:18.704 --> 17:21.039
‎But what would that accomplish?

17:21.040 --> 17:25.168
‎If they wanted me out of the race,
‎it's as good as done.

17:25.169 --> 17:27.378
‎My horse, my saddle...
‎everything's gone.

17:27.379 --> 17:29.339
‎Gyro's gear and horse too.

17:31.550 --> 17:33.302
‎Are they looking for

17:33.886 --> 17:35.595
‎something?

17:35.596 --> 17:39.348
‎They went after Gyro first,
‎then my horse and gear...

17:39.349 --> 17:42.728
‎And now they won't stop coming after me.

17:43.771 --> 17:47.691
‎Because they think we're hiding something.

17:48.817 --> 17:51.570
‎Then what are they looking for?

17:53.030 --> 17:55.324
‎The thing that could be valuable is...

17:58.952 --> 18:02.288
‎They ignored Gyro's Steel Ball.

18:02.289 --> 18:04.541
‎I don't have anything but my horse...

18:05.167 --> 18:11.048
‎No way... Could it be
‎that mummified left arm I saw?

18:11.757 --> 18:13.884
‎So it wasn't a hallucination.

18:14.426 --> 18:17.678
‎Oye... Stroheim too...

18:17.679 --> 18:22.768
‎Not just them. The terrorists
‎are all after the arm inside my hand!

18:23.352 --> 18:26.145
‎What is that mummified arm?

18:26.146 --> 18:28.816
‎Just whose arm is it?

18:44.123 --> 18:50.170
‎Whir, whir, whir...

18:54.383 --> 18:56.760
‎Ka-plunk!

18:57.511 --> 19:01.223
‎Creak... Ka-plunk!

19:03.308 --> 19:04.935
‎Grab.

19:07.563 --> 19:08.564
‎Huh?

19:14.653 --> 19:15.779
‎Sniff, sniff, sniff...

19:17.865 --> 19:20.534
‎Pop! Slurp, slurp, slurp...

19:21.410 --> 19:22.493
‎That's good!

19:22.494 --> 19:24.203
‎Creak... Ka-plunk!

19:24.204 --> 19:26.247
‎But it's not here.

19:26.248 --> 19:28.791
‎It's not in this gear either!

19:28.792 --> 19:30.459
‎So that means...

19:30.460 --> 19:33.713
‎Johnee... What was his name again?

19:33.714 --> 19:35.214
‎Joshter.

19:35.215 --> 19:37.341
‎Johnee Joshter.

19:37.342 --> 19:40.052
‎He's carrying it himself.

19:40.053 --> 19:44.015
‎That settles it!
‎He's got it hidden somewhere on him!

19:44.016 --> 19:46.768
‎Ka-plunk! Creak... Ka-plunk!

20:07.080 --> 20:08.248
‎No way...

20:08.916 --> 20:11.209
‎Gyro, where are you?

20:11.210 --> 20:13.253
‎Are you alive? Or are you dead?

20:14.296 --> 20:18.592
‎I only wanted to learn
‎the secret of your Steel Ball.

20:19.134 --> 20:22.136
‎Ever since that strange arm
‎attached itself to me.

20:22.137 --> 20:25.265
‎Damn it!
‎If I leave this place, they'll kill me.

20:25.891 --> 20:28.142
‎Gyro, help me.

20:28.143 --> 20:29.728
‎What am I supposed to do?

20:33.440 --> 20:36.025
‎No vacancy here.

20:36.026 --> 20:38.904
‎We're fully booked for months!

20:46.745 --> 20:48.455
‎What the...

20:49.081 --> 20:51.040
‎It's not just the feather!

20:51.041 --> 20:53.585
‎This ability is a lure!

20:56.129 --> 20:58.131
‎I've got to get the hook out!

20:58.632 --> 21:00.008
‎Hurry...

21:02.636 --> 21:04.429
‎What?

21:14.356 --> 21:16.608
‎I'm done for!

21:17.985 --> 21:21.697
‎They're going to kill me.
‎Once they realized it's inside me...

21:22.614 --> 21:23.740
‎Then...

21:24.324 --> 21:25.783
‎You can have it!

21:25.784 --> 21:28.452
‎If you want it that badly,
‎you can have it!

21:28.453 --> 21:30.871
‎It's not like I wanted it
‎in the first place!

21:30.872 --> 21:33.249
‎I don't need this thing!

21:33.250 --> 21:35.168
‎Just take it!

21:47.347 --> 21:57.774
‎Movēre crūs.

21:58.483 --> 21:59.484
‎What the...

23:30.951 --> 23:35.956
‎Subtitle translation by: Ryoko Quirke
